<!--Post: 4527--><!--Time: 1106485781-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4527"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 5:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was just reading Tom&#39;s new section with the out takes of the letters. In BTK&#39;s list of serial killers he names &#34;panty hose killer in florida&#34; does anyone know what case he is referencing. I gather the killer had not been apprehended yet like his &#34;ted of the west coast&#34; he refers to only what was known or written in the papers. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4527-->
<!--Post: 4688--><!--Time: 1106678430-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4688"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:Iwillc@tchu.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 10:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I found the following article from a 1966 unsolved homicide.  <a href="http://www.fdle.state.fl.us/osi/unsolved/Sims1A.asp" target=_top>http://www.fdle.state.fl.us/osi/unsolved/Sims1A.as p</a> <BR>The crime seems earily similar to some of BTK&#39;s methodology, but I doubt it is related.  It does mention a stocking though.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4688-->
<!--Post: 4788--><!--Time: 1106751653-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4788"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lazysean<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lazysean<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 7:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have read before -- and consider it a very strong possibility -- that the &#34;Panty Hose Strangler of Florida&#34; and &#34;Ted of the West Coast&#34; are really one and the same.  Look at the time frame -- this letter was sent in early February 1978, about three weeks after Ted&#39;s Chi Omega/Cheryl Thomas attacks in Tallahassee Fl on January 15.  Two of the Chi Omega girls had been strangled with a stocking, and a pantyhose mask was found at Thomas&#39;s.  At the time, though, no one knew it was Bundy.  He had escaped custody in Colorado in December and would not be recaptured until a few days after this letter was received. <BR> <BR>A recent headline involving multiple strangulations of young girls on the Otero anniversary?  How could BTK pass that up? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4788-->
<!--Post: 4796--><!--Time: 1106755795-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4796"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 8:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks Lazy, I had considered Chi Omega as the crime he was talking about. I did not realize it was so close to the date of the letter being sent. I&#39;m terrible with dates. That is very intresting about them being so close. It&#39;s as if he felt someone was getting more press then him and was jealous.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4796-->
<!--Post: 4799--><!--Time: 1106756166-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4799"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 8:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;this letter was sent in early February 1978, about three weeks after Ted&#39;s Chi Omega/Cheryl Thomas attacks in Tallahassee Fl on January 15. Two of the Chi Omega girls had been strangled with a stocking, and a pantyhose mask was found at Thomas&#39;s. At the time, though, no one knew it was Bundy.&#34; <BR> <BR>So BTK reads the paper...he also refered to the 3 dudes in jail in an earlier letter, which he found out through the paper...also &#34;until I read their names in the paper&#34;...wonder how long the Wichita Eagle has kept thier subscriber list? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4799-->
<!--Post: 7352--><!--Time: 1108418740-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7352"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 2:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I thought Ted of the West Coast meant that BTK considered Ted Bundy&#39;s serial killings on the West to be masterpieces, while he messed up and got caught in Florida. Now I know. <BR> <BR>One thing for certain, these things freak me out, so, I won&#39;t be wearing pantyhose anymore! <BR> <BR><IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7352-->
<!--Post: 7358--><!--Time: 1108422235-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7358"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 3:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ted Bundy entered the Chi Omega sorority house in the early hours of January 15 1978. He murdered Margaret Bowman and Lisa Levy. Kathy Kleiner and Karen Chandler were injured in the attack. Within an hour of the Chi Omega murders, Bundy entered the home of Cheryl Thomas, another university student and murdered her with a blunt weapon. <BR> <BR>The BTK Strangler&#39;s desire for recognition as a successful serial murderer prompted the references to other serial murderers. The unknown subject wanted the police and the public to perceive him in the same breath as Ted Bundy and David Berkowitz. The BTK Strangler sought to project the threatening shadow of a sadistic psychopathic serial murderer and the presence of an infamous criminal.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7358-->
